{"title":"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <i>arithmetic sequence</i> is a sequence in which each term after the first is obtained from the previous term by adding a constant. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/b/18b109bbad8ddff023f591be8a7ed806fdcc5938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5, 7, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> is an arithmetic sequence with three terms.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Parts\">Parts</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Parts\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_A\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part A\">2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part A</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_B\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part B\">2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part B</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_C\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part C\">2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part C</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_D\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part D\">2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part D</a></